WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.167
-It is great to see you.
We love it when you come by.

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:04.868
Always looking good, bud.
-I love being here, man.

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:06.300
-Always a stud.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.501
By the way, speaking of studs,
look at this cover of "Esquire."

00:00:08.501 --> 00:00:10.234
If anyone saw this.
Look at this.

00:00:10.234 --> 00:00:11.767
Hey, that's what
I'm talking about.

00:00:11.767 --> 00:00:14.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:16.601
No, just wait.

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:19.133
And I think you know
what photo I'm going to show.

00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:22.767
I'm reading about ya.
I go, "Oh, cool, I saw."

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:26.133
And then we had the page marked
and blocked off as well because.

00:00:26.133 --> 00:00:30.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:33.634
What is going through your mind
when you go,

00:00:33.634 --> 00:00:35.667
"Oh, maybe I'll try this?"
-Yeah.

00:00:35.667 --> 00:00:38.834
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:40.801
I was a fan of the photo.

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:43.100
It was inspired by the
Red Hot Chili Peppers.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.000
I don't know if you guys are
familiar with the photo.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.033
But they used to put on shows

00:00:47.033 --> 00:00:49.167
wearing just only a sock
all the time.

00:00:49.167 --> 00:00:52.367
And, you know, I just wanted
something kind of

00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:54.334
like shocking for this cover.

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:59.067
-You got it.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:01.567
I want to talk about
also the album, by the way.

00:01:01.567 --> 00:01:04.567
We have to talk about this.
I love the cover art right here.

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:06.200
Gorgeous.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.267
But also you were in a movie
earlier this year called "X."

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:13.968
-Yeah.
-And I know that your mom is

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:16.167
a giant fan of your stuff,
and you go,

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:18.067
"Well, maybe, Mom, you can't see
this one."

00:01:18.067 --> 00:01:19.434
-Yeah, this one I was like,
"No, you can't."

00:01:19.434 --> 00:01:21.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:23.400
-I mean, the "Esquire" picture
is nothing.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.234
-No. I mean, she's seen
"Esquire,"

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:28.868
but I don't know what she thinks
about that one photo.

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:31.133
She kind of just like didn't say
anything about it.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:33.834
-This is the one thing
that she can't see.

00:01:33.834 --> 00:01:36.234
You go, "Here's the movie, Mom,
but you can't see this.

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:37.734
Just trust me, it's good."
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:37.734 --> 00:01:41.133
But she was hearing all these
good things about it and,

00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:43.434
you know, she was just like,
"Man, I want to see it."

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:48.334
And I was, like, "Well, let me
hit up Ti West and see if

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:51.434
it's possible to make like
a mommy edit of the movie..."

00:01:51.434 --> 00:01:52.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.934 --> 00:01:56.167
..."that has no sex included
at all

00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:59.868
and it's just nothing
but gore and madness."

00:01:59.868 --> 00:02:01.767
So he said, "Let me see
what I can do."

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:03.501
And he hit me up two days later,
and he was like,

00:02:03.501 --> 00:02:05.300
"What's your mom's address? I'm
going to send it to her house."

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:06.501
-No way.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:06.501 --> 00:02:07.601
-So he really made a mom edit
just for you?

00:02:07.601 --> 00:02:08.868
-He made a mommy edit.

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:10.300
I call it the mommy edit.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.100
-That's a good man.

00:02:13.234 --> 00:02:15.000
That's a good dude right there.

00:02:16.968 --> 00:02:19.300
I'd never heard the word
"Entergalactic"

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.300
before as one word.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.467
But you were telling me
backstage, you go,

00:02:24.467 --> 00:02:26.934
"Yeah, I think I actually
created a different language

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:29.200
as well with my daughter."

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:30.334
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:30.334 --> 00:02:31.834
-And I go,
"What are you talking about?"

00:02:31.834 --> 00:02:33.400
You showed me this.
And it's very interesting.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.934
Do you have a name
for the language yet?

00:02:34.934 --> 00:02:36.067
-No, not yet.

00:02:36.067 --> 00:02:38.133
-No, because it's just starting
really.

00:02:38.133 --> 00:02:40.734
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-It's like meeping almost.

00:02:40.734 --> 00:02:43.200
-Yeah, kind of like Road Runner.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.501
-Yeah, meep, like "meep, meep."

00:02:44.501 --> 00:02:46.334
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:46.334 --> 00:02:47.801
-So it just started with what?

00:02:47.801 --> 00:02:49.467
How did this start meeping?

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:53.567
-I send my daughter
silly messages all the time.

00:02:53.567 --> 00:02:55.434
Sometimes I'll just send her
voice notes where I'm like...

00:02:55.434 --> 00:02:57.667
[ Shouting gibberish ]

00:02:57.667 --> 00:02:59.868
For no reason.

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:02.968
-Sounds like a goat in pain.

00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:05.934
-And she's just like,
"Hi, Daddy." You know?

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:09.100
But I was like, "Man, I just
want to send her something.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.067
I just want to play with her and
see if she can pick up on it."

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:13.434
And I sent "Meep, meep."

00:03:13.434 --> 00:03:15.367
And she responded like, "Meep."

00:03:15.367 --> 00:03:17.200
And I was like, "Oh, I got her,
I got her."

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:19.400
So I kept going with it.
I was like, "Meep, meep morpus."

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.868
And then she responded,
"Meep, meep, morpus, morpus."

00:03:21.868 --> 00:03:23.534
And I was like, "Okay, okay.

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:25.033
Let me spice it up
a little bit."

00:03:25.033 --> 00:03:28.067
I sent, "Meep meeps poos.
Meeps poopis morpus."

00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:29.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:31.300
Meaning like, I [bleep]
my pants.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.100
-Okay, alright.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.133
Again, we're going to have to

00:03:34.133 --> 00:03:35.434
edit a lot of things
for your mom.

00:03:35.434 --> 00:03:36.934
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:39.033
This is the thing.

00:03:39.033 --> 00:03:41.067
This is actually a text from you
and your daughter.

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:44.200
-Yeah.
-So this "mi meep--"

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.334
-"Meep meep merp merp meep.

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:48.133
Mi meeps mu muu."

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:50.467
Because I say "mi meeps mu."
That's "I love you."

00:03:50.467 --> 00:03:52.400
And she says, "I love you too."

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:57.267
And then thanks -- "muu meeps."

00:03:57.267 --> 00:03:58.734
And she says, "mo mulem."

00:03:58.734 --> 00:04:00.901
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.901 --> 00:04:03.601
-"Mo mulem,"
you're welcome, yeah.

00:04:03.601 --> 00:04:07.801
Mi mi -- Mi mi meepies,
which I think means very funny.

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:09.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.567 --> 00:04:11.567
Let's talk about
"Entergalactic," please.

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:13.133
This is your 10th studio album.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:14.901
It comes out on Friday.

00:04:14.901 --> 00:04:16.934
Also your TV special
"Entergalactic"

00:04:16.934 --> 00:04:18.300
is on Netflix Friday.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:21.033
How do these projects about
and which one came first?

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:23.634
-Well, the music came first.

00:04:23.634 --> 00:04:27.300
I was kind of like bored of
doing the same old thing

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.801
with albums, like kind of
releasing an album,

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:31.701
doing two or three music videos
tops

00:04:31.701 --> 00:04:33.434
and then that'd be
the end of it.

00:04:33.434 --> 00:04:34.934
I wanted something,

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:39.100
just a bigger splash this time
around, you know?

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:43.267
And I thought about the idea
to splice the music

00:04:43.267 --> 00:04:47.801
with the animation but have the
music kind of narrate the story.

00:04:47.801 --> 00:04:49.968
You know, something that hasn't
really been done before.

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:51.567
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:54.701
And that's kind of why we've
been calling it a TV event.

00:04:54.701 --> 00:04:56.067
-You're always doing something
different.

00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:59.334
I love that you just keep going,
something else different.

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:00.934
-I try to push it.
I always try to push it.

00:05:00.934 --> 00:05:02.834
-Yeah, and you got some good
friends that come in

00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:05.667
and do voices in this special.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:07.801
I just reached out to people
that I knew,

00:05:07.801 --> 00:05:12.634
people that I love and see if
they would do a favor for me.

00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:14.367
-I mean, Timothee Chalamet
is in it.

00:05:14.367 --> 00:05:16.167
-Yeah, yeah.
-That's fun.

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:17.801
You just call him and say,
"Timothee, let's do this."

00:05:17.801 --> 00:05:19.367
-Yeah, I was talking to him
about it,

00:05:19.367 --> 00:05:21.033
and he said it sounded cool.

00:05:21.033 --> 00:05:24.400
And over the years, when things
started to pick up, I was like,

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.234
"Hey, man, you're going to get
an offer

00:05:26.234 --> 00:05:28.067
one day to do this show.

00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:29.834
I was serious about you
doing this."

00:05:29.834 --> 00:05:32.067
And he's like, "No, I'm serious.
I want to do it."

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:34.234
-So he did it.
-And he got the scripts.

00:05:34.234 --> 00:05:36.067
We sent him everything.
He loved it.

00:05:36.067 --> 00:05:38.968
'Cause that's the thing, you
know -- I never want my friends

00:05:38.968 --> 00:05:42.501
to feel like I'm going to lead
them into some bull[bleep].

00:05:42.501 --> 00:05:45.667
I kind of wanted to let them
know like, "This is dope."

00:05:45.667 --> 00:05:48.634
-"You can trust me."
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:48.634 --> 00:05:50.934
"-I'm going to make it cool.
I'll make it look good."

00:05:50.934 --> 00:05:53.801
Can you explain the story about
the Netflix special?

00:05:53.801 --> 00:05:57.300
-Well, pretty much it's about --
it starts with this guy, Jabari,

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:59.501
who just moved into his
apartment and got a new job

00:05:59.501 --> 00:06:02.334
working at this comic book
company

00:06:02.334 --> 00:06:05.767
to develop his character
into a comic book.

00:06:05.767 --> 00:06:09.400
And he meets this young lady,
Meadow, who ends up

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:11.801
being his neighbor down the hall
from him.

00:06:11.801 --> 00:06:14.734
And he has, like, this instant
connection with her.

00:06:14.734 --> 00:06:18.100
And the show is pretty much
about their relationship,

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:20.033
and will they or won't they,
you know?

00:06:20.033 --> 00:06:21.701
-Yeah, I want to show everyone
a clip.

00:06:21.701 --> 00:06:24.601
Here's Kid Cudi in his Netflix
special "Entergalactic."

00:06:24.601 --> 00:06:25.968
Take a look at this.

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:28.667
-What's up?
-Right.

00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:32.367
Uh, so I just want to apologize
for last night.

00:06:32.367 --> 00:06:33.801
I feel so bad.

00:06:33.801 --> 00:06:35.934
I did not mean for things to get
so out of control.

00:06:35.934 --> 00:06:38.067
-It's all good. All good.

00:06:38.067 --> 00:06:40.567
I can't be mad at a Friday night
turn-up.

00:06:40.567 --> 00:06:42.934
But I can be mad at your music.

00:06:42.934 --> 00:06:45.934
-Uh, I'm sorry?

00:06:45.934 --> 00:06:48.100
-Yeah. Was that Drew Hill?

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:51.133
-Okay, pre-"Thong Song" Sisqo
was fire.

00:06:51.133 --> 00:06:53.801
-Yeah, but never forget
post-"Thong Song" Sisqo.

00:06:53.801 --> 00:06:56.167
-Fair.

00:06:56.167 --> 00:06:58.400
-Post-"Thong Song."

00:06:58.400 --> 00:07:00.701
♪ Thong, thong,
thong, thong, thong ♪

00:07:00.701 --> 00:07:03.868
-Hold on, man.
We love Sisqo. We love Sisqo.

00:07:03.868 --> 00:07:06.300
Don't get it twisted.
-Yeah, don't get it twisted.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.200
Kid Cudi, everybody.

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:11.033
"Entergalactic" is on Netflix
this Friday.

00:07:11.033 --> 00:07:14.901
His new album "Entergalactic"
is also out Friday.

00:07:14.901 --> 00:07:17.534
When we come back, he's
performing with Ty Dolla $ign.

00:07:17.534 --> 00:07:19.133
Kid Cudi!

